of it is substations and transformers (utility-capex-2027).\n- **Pellham's offering:** Pellham withdrew its planned C$2.4B equity offering because investor demand fell short. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering). That is direct evidence that equity failed for the largest utility, and the shortfall is already reducing capex.\n- **Wider equity market:** Equity markets have been less receptive, and two other utility share offerings were cut back in size (utility-credit, Q3 2026).\n- **Debt as the alternative:** Bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Even so, Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (utility-credit). Debt looks more workable than equity, though it costs more.\n\n**Implication:** Utilities that need to fund the planned increases will probably lean on debt. Equity-dependent plans, especially Pellham's, are likely to be scaled back or deferred. This is negative for grid-equipment demand from Pellham, the largest single buyer in Caldria.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on utility share prices, valuations, or Norvane's own equity needs. I also don't know whether Pellham plans to retry the offering.","ttft_ms":2352,"type":"result","duration_ms":16901,"uuid":"a5bbef64-2b2f-4f32-87f4-3da684c3b4b7","ttft_stream_ms":1205,"time_to_request_ms":112,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":4,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":4,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":10,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":62,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":60,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"proce